+**Background work with nobody watching.** A `terminal(background=true,
+notify_on_complete=true)` process that exits, or a background subagent
+(`delegate_task`) that finishes, while its CLI, TUI or Desktop session has no
+viewer is written into the session as a note, and the next turn reads it. To
+have the agent pick the work back up on its own, set
+`sessions.unviewed_completion_turns` to the number of such completions a
+session may run as agent turns in a row with no viewer (default `0`: notes
+only). Process exits and subagent results share one count:
+
+```yaml
+sessions:
+  unviewed_completion_turns: 20
+```
+
+The turn runs and is saved like any other, so a client that attaches later
+sees it in the history. A viewer attaching or a message from you starts the
+count again (so does a gateway restart); past the limit, completions are notes
+until then. A chat you closed (exit or `/new`) keeps notes, and so does the
+result of a subagent whose session was closed. A session the gateway
+ended because its viewer vanished is reopened for the turn and ended again
+`sessions.orphan_end_grace_s` after the turn starts, or when it settles if
+that is later. Watch-pattern notices are not affected, and neither are
+messaging chats, whose completions always start a turn.
